  "description": "Wide Tokyo JR schematic using the station-numbering map's corridor arrangement: the complete 30-station Yamanote loop has straight sides, balanced diagonal shoulders and centered, shorter northern and southern shelves. Tokaido runs west from Shinagawa through Yokohama to Ofuna, then folds north through Chigasaki and back to Odawara rather than extending far south. Shonan-Shinjuku includes Tokaido-bound rapid and Yokosuka-bound local services to Odawara and Zushi, cropped north at Akabane. Rapid is not special rapid: it serves all Tokaido stations south of Totsuka. Other adjacent corridors retain their named cropped boundaries; these are not necessarily real service termini. Keihin-Tohoku uses its local stopping pattern on its own row beside the Tokaido axis. The Tokyo Monorail runs from Hamamatsucho along the bay to Haneda Airport Terminal 2. No subway, northern regional branches, Keikyu airport line or timetable simulation. Original schematic geometry, not copied map artwork.",
